  "keyPoints": {
    "en": [
      "Kiwami 2 uses the Dragon Engine (same as Yakuza 6), which replaces style-switching with a unified combat system—fluid transitions between grab attacks and strikes replace discrete stance changes.",
      "The new physics-based combat allows environmental interaction: chairs, bikes, traffic signs, and scaffolding can all be grabbed and used as weapons mid-combo.",
      "Kiryu's Heat Actions in Kiwami 2 are tied to surroundings—near a wall triggers different Heat Actions than in open space; memorize environment-specific executions for maximum damage.",
      "The Cabaret Club Grand Prix mini-game is a significant content stream; recruiting and leveling hostesses through its management layers provides large EXP and money rewards.",
      "Completion percentage includes the Majima Story (Majima Construction chapters); these can be played independently and contribute to overall completion requirements."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "極2はドラゴンエンジン（龍が如く6と同じ）を使用。スタイル切り替えを統合戦闘システムに置き換え、グラブ攻撃とストライクのスムーズな移行が個別スタンス変更に替わる。",
      "新しい物理ベースの戦闘で環境インタラクションが可能。椅子・自転車・交通標識・足場など全てをコンボ中の武器として掴める。",
      "極2の桐生のヒートアクションは周囲に連動。壁の近くでは開けた場所と異なるヒートアクションが発動。環境固有の処刑技を記憶し最大ダメージを狙う。",
      "キャバレークラブGPミニゲームは重要コンテンツ。経営レイヤーを通じてホステスを採用・育成すると大きなEXPと資金報酬が得られる。",
      "コンプリート率には真島篇（真島組章）が含まれる。独立してプレイ可能で全体コンプリート要件に寄与する。"
    ]
  },
  "opening": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Dragon Engine Combat Fundamentals",
        "body": "Unlike previous Yakuza titles, Kiwami 2 uses a unified combat flow. Focus on learning the dodge/evasion timing (one dodge button rather than multiple style-specific evasions) and the standard combo to Heat Action transition. Environmental awareness is critical—position Kiryu near walls, poles, or furniture before initiating combos to access higher-damage Heat Action variants that are only available with obstacles nearby."
      }
    ]
  },
  "midGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Cabaret Club Management",
        "body": "The Cabaret Club Grand Prix is a real-time strategy layer within Kiwami 2. Recruit hostesses from the city, assign them to tables based on customer type preferences, and manage shift rotations to maximize nightly revenue. Investing in hostess rank-ups (via lessons and gifts) unlocks special abilities that dramatically increase single-table revenue. Winning the Grand Prix provides access to some of the best equipment in the game."
      }
    ]
  },
  "endGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Substory Completion and Legend Difficulty",
        "body": "Full substory completion in Kamurocho and Sotenbori is required for 100%. Substory locations are marked on the map after speaking to NPC characters in each area; some substories trigger only at specific story chapters. Legend difficulty (unlocked after completing Normal) provides the most challenging combat scenarios and exclusive rewards, serving as the post-game test for mastered Dragon Engine technique."
      }
    ]
  },
  "mistakes": {
    "en": [
      "Not exploring both cities (Kamurocho and Sotenbori)—Kiwami 2 features two full city maps; spending time only in Kamurocho misses half the substory content and shops in Sotenbori.",
      "Neglecting the hostess recruitment system—even casual participation in the Cabaret Club provides large EXP injections that accelerate Kiryu's upgrade path significantly.",
      "Using grab attacks against enemies in groups—grabbing in a crowd exposes Kiryu to flank attacks from other enemies; use crowd control Heat Actions to stagger groups before engaging individuals.",
      "Missing the Mr. Shakedown encounters—these massive enemies provide massive EXP when defeated and respawn repeatedly throughout the game; farming them funds the entire upgrade tree.",
      "Skipping the Majima Story chapters—Majima's segments provide significant backstory to the main narrative and completing them early contextualizes Chapter 12's plot reveals better."
    ],
